module

public import Mathlib.FieldTheory.Galois.GaloisClosure
public import Mathlib.FieldTheory.Galois.Profinite
public import Mathlib.FieldTheory.IsSepClosed
public import Mathlib.FieldTheory.KrullTopology
public import Mathlib.RepresentationTheory.Homological.GroupCohomology.LowDegree
public import Mathlib.Topology.LocallyConstant.Basic

/-!
# Continuous `2`-cocycles of an infinite Galois group come from a finite level

Let `Ω/K` be a Galois extension, possibly infinite, and let `f : Gal(Ω/K) × Gal(Ω/K) → Ωˣ` be a
continuous `2`-cocycle, continuity being local constancy because `Ωˣ` is a discrete Galois
module. This file shows that `f` is the *inflation* of a `2`-cocycle on a finite Galois
subextension: there are a finite Galois `L/K` inside `Ω` and a `2`-cocycle
`F : Gal(L/K) × Gal(L/K) → Lˣ` with `f (g, h) = F (g|_L, h|_L)` for all `g, h`.

The immediate consequence is a reduction of the vanishing of the second continuous cohomology
group `H²(Gal(Ω/K), Ωˣ)` to the vanishing of the finite-level groups `H²(Gal(L/K), Lˣ)`. For
`Ω = Kˢᵉᵖ` this is the step that
[Stacks, Tag 03R8](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03R8) uses in degree `2`: the hypothesis
of that proposition controls the Brauer groups of the *finite* extensions of `K`, and the
finite-level groups `H²(Gal(L/K), Lˣ)` are what the Brauer groups compute.

## Main results

* `Stacks.GaloisCohomology.exists_intermediateField_eq_of_isLocallyConstant`: a locally constant
  function on `Gal(Ω/K) × Gal(Ω/K)` is invariant under translating both arguments by
  `Gal(Ω/E)`, for a single finite subextension `E/K`. The target is an arbitrary type, so this is
  available for the cochains of any discrete Galois module.
* `Stacks.GaloisCohomology.exists_isMulCocycle₂_inflation`: every locally constant `2`-cocycle
  `Gal(Ω/K) × Gal(Ω/K) → Ωˣ` is `inflation₂ L F` for a finite Galois subextension `L/K` and a
  `2`-cocycle `F : Gal(L/K) × Gal(L/K) → Lˣ`.
* `Stacks.GaloisCohomology.isMulCocycle₂_inflation₂` and
  `Stacks.GaloisCohomology.isLocallyConstant_inflation₂`: conversely, inflation takes
  `2`-cocycles to locally constant `2`-cocycles.
* `Stacks.GaloisCohomology.isMulCoboundary₂_of_forall_finiteGalois`: if at every finite Galois
  level every `2`-cocycle is a coboundary, then every locally constant `2`-cocycle on
  `Gal(Ω/K)` is a coboundary. `isMulCoboundary₂_of_continuous_of_forall_finiteGalois` spells the
  cochain condition as continuity, and
  `isMulCoboundary₂_separableClosure_of_forall_finiteGalois` is the case `Ω = Kˢᵉᵖ`.
* `Stacks.GaloisCohomology.exists_isLocallyConstant_isMulCoboundary₂_of_forall_finiteGalois`: the
  same conclusion with the local constancy of the trivialising `1`-cochain recorded, the cochain
  being `Stacks.GaloisCohomology.isLocallyConstant_inflation₁` of a cochain at a finite level.
  This is the form the degree-two comparison between the cocycle and derived-functor descriptions
  of Galois cohomology needs; see the implementation notes.

## Implementation notes

The cocycle and coboundary conditions are Mathlib's `IsMulCocycle₂` and `IsMulCoboundary₂`, as
in the degree-one file `Hilbert90`. Mathlib's bridge between
`IsMulCocycle₂` and `groupCohomology.cocycles₂`, namely `cocyclesOfIsMulCocycle₂` and the
lemmas beside it, is stated only for a group and a module in `Type 0`, whereas `Gal(Ω/K)` lives
in the universe of `Ω`. Phrasing the statements with `IsMulCocycle₂` also avoids transporting
`Ωˣ` into the additive category `Rep ℤ Gal(Ω/K)`.

The repository's derived-functor `continuousGroupCohomology` has a cocycle description above
degree zero, not only the comparison `invariantsIsoZerothCohomology`: degrees one and two are
compared in
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.EtaleCohomology.GroupCohomology.DegreeOneCocycles` and
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.EtaleCohomology.GroupCohomology.DegreeTwoCocycles`. The
degree-two comparison consumes a *locally constant* trivialising `1`-cochain, which is more than
`IsMulCoboundary₂` provides, so
`Stacks.GaloisCohomology.exists_isLocallyConstant_isMulCoboundary₂_of_forall_finiteGalois` below
records that the cochain produced here, being inflated from a finite level, is locally
constant.

The reduction has two halves. Local constancy makes each fibre of `f` open, which by the
neighbourhood basis of the Krull topology gives, for each point of `Gal(Ω/K) × Gal(Ω/K)`
separately, a finite subextension whose fixing subgroup translates that point without changing
the value of `f`; compactness of `Gal(Ω/K) × Gal(Ω/K)` — the Galois group of a Galois extension
is profinite — turns this into a single subextension working at every point. Separately, a
locally constant function on a compact space has finite range, so the values of `f` generate a
finite subextension. Enlarging to the join of the normal closure of the first field and the
finite Galois field generated by the values gives one finite Galois `L/K` which both makes `f`
factor through `Gal(L/K) × Gal(L/K)` and contains all values of `f`. A finite Galois
subextension is packaged as Mathlib's `FiniteGaloisIntermediateField`, whose instance fields
supply the finiteness and Galois instances that `AlgEquiv.restrictNormalHom` needs.

What this file does *not* do is identify the finite-level groups `H²(Gal(L/K), Lˣ)` with
relative Brauer groups, which is the remaining content of
[Stacks, Tag 03R7](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03R7): that identification is the
crossed-product construction, and neither crossed products nor factor systems exist in Mathlib
or in this repository. Accordingly no `@[stacks]` tag is claimed here.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 03R7](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03R7), whose surjectivity
  argument begins with the reduction proved here.
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03R8](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03R8), whose degree-`2`
  vanishing is reduced here to the finite levels.
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open IntermediateField groupCohomology
open scoped Topology

namespace Stacks.GaloisCohomology

variable {K Ω : Type*} [Field K] [Field Ω] [Algebra K Ω] [IsGalois K Ω]

omit [IsGalois K Ω] in
/-- A locally constant function on `Gal(Ω/K) × Gal(Ω/K)` is unchanged when its two arguments are
multiplied on the right by elements of `Gal(Ω/E)`, for some finite subextension `E/K` depending
on the chosen point.

The fibre of `f` through the point is open, so translating it back to the identity exhibits an
open neighbourhood of `(1, 1)`; a basic neighbourhood of `1` in the Krull topology is the fixing
subgroup of a finite subextension, and one such subgroup works in both coordinates. -/
theorem exists_intermediateField_eq_of_isLocallyConstant_apply {α : Type*}
    (f : Gal(Ω/K) × Gal(Ω/K) → α) (hf : IsLocallyConstant f) (p : Gal(Ω/K) × Gal(Ω/K)) :
    ∃ E : IntermediateField K Ω, FiniteDimensional K E ∧
      ∀ a b : Gal(Ω/K), a ∈ E.fixingSubgroup → b ∈ E.fixingSubgroup →
        f (p.1 * a, p.2 * b) = f p := by
  set T : Set (Gal(Ω/K) × Gal(Ω/K)) :=
    (fun q : Gal(Ω/K) × Gal(Ω/K) => (p.1 * q.1, p.2 * q.2)) ⁻¹' (f ⁻¹' {f p}) with hTdef
  have hTopen : IsOpen T :=
    (hf {f p}).preimage
      ((continuous_const.mul continuous_fst).prodMk (continuous_const.mul continuous_snd))
  have hmem : T ∈ 𝓝 ((1 : Gal(Ω/K)), (1 : Gal(Ω/K))) := hTopen.mem_nhds (by simp [hTdef])
  rw [nhds_prod_eq] at hmem
  obtain ⟨U, hU, V, hV, hUV⟩ := Filter.mem_prod_iff.1 hmem
  obtain ⟨E, hE, hEsub⟩ :=
    (krullTopology_mem_nhds_one_iff K Ω (U ∩ V)).1 (Filter.inter_mem hU hV)
  exact ⟨E, hE, fun a b ha hb => hUV (Set.mk_mem_prod (hEsub ha).1 (hEsub hb).2)⟩

/-- A locally constant function on `Gal(Ω/K) × Gal(Ω/K)` is unchanged when its two arguments are
multiplied on the right by elements of `Gal(Ω/E)`, for a *single* finite subextension `E/K`: in
other words, it factors through `Gal(E'/K) × Gal(E'/K)` for a finite level `E'`.

The pointwise statement `exists_intermediateField_eq_of_isLocallyConstant_apply` gives an open
cover of `Gal(Ω/K) × Gal(Ω/K)` by products of cosets of fixing subgroups on which `f` is
constant. The Galois group of a Galois extension is compact, so finitely many of these suffice,
and a fixing subgroup contained in each of the finitely many is again the fixing subgroup of a
finite subextension because they are all neighbourhoods of `1`. -/
theorem exists_intermediateField_eq_of_isLocallyConstant {α : Type*}
    (f : Gal(Ω/K) × Gal(Ω/K) → α) (hf : IsLocallyConstant f) :
    ∃ E : IntermediateField K Ω, FiniteDimensional K E ∧
      ∀ σ τ a b : Gal(Ω/K), a ∈ E.fixingSubgroup → b ∈ E.fixingSubgroup →
        f (σ * a, τ * b) = f (σ, τ) := by
  choose E hEfin hEprop using exists_intermediateField_eq_of_isLocallyConstant_apply f hf
  set W : Gal(Ω/K) × Gal(Ω/K) → Set (Gal(Ω/K) × Gal(Ω/K)) := fun p =>
    (fun q : Gal(Ω/K) × Gal(Ω/K) => (p.1⁻¹ * q.1, p.2⁻¹ * q.2)) ⁻¹'
      (((E p).fixingSubgroup : Set Gal(Ω/K)) ×ˢ ((E p).fixingSubgroup : Set Gal(Ω/K)))
    with hWdef
  have hWopen : ∀ p, IsOpen (W p) := fun p => by
    have := hEfin p
    exact (((E p).fixingSubgroup_isOpen).prod ((E p).fixingSubgroup_isOpen)).preimage
      ((continuous_const.mul continuous_fst).prodMk (continuous_const.mul continuous_snd))
  have hWself : ∀ p, p ∈ W p := fun p => by simp [hWdef, one_mem]
  obtain ⟨t, ht⟩ := isCompact_univ.elim_finite_subcover W hWopen
    fun p _ => Set.mem_iUnion.2 ⟨p, hWself p⟩
  have hnhd : (⋂ p ∈ (t : Set (Gal(Ω/K) × Gal(Ω/K))),
      ((E p).fixingSubgroup : Set Gal(Ω/K))) ∈ 𝓝 (1 : Gal(Ω/K)) :=
    (Filter.biInter_mem t.finite_toSet).2 fun p _ =>
      (krullTopology_mem_nhds_one_iff K Ω _).2 ⟨E p, hEfin p, subset_rfl⟩
  obtain ⟨F, hFfin, hFsub⟩ := (krullTopology_mem_nhds_one_iff K Ω _).1 hnhd
  refine ⟨F, hFfin, fun σ τ a b ha hb => ?_⟩
  obtain ⟨p, hpt, hp⟩ := Set.mem_iUnion₂.1 (ht (Set.mem_univ (σ, τ)))
  have ha' : a ∈ (E p).fixingSubgroup := Set.mem_iInter₂.1 (hFsub ha) p hpt
  have hb' : b ∈ (E p).fixingSubgroup := Set.mem_iInter₂.1 (hFsub hb) p hpt
  have hσ : p.1⁻¹ * σ ∈ (E p).fixingSubgroup := hp.1
  have hτ : p.2⁻¹ * τ ∈ (E p).fixingSubgroup := hp.2
  have h1 : f (σ * a, τ * b) = f p := by
    have := hEprop p _ _ (mul_mem hσ ha') (mul_mem hτ hb')
    rwa [show p.1 * (p.1⁻¹ * σ * a) = σ * a by group,
      show p.2 * (p.2⁻¹ * τ * b) = τ * b by group] at this
  have h2 : f (σ, τ) = f p := by
    have := hEprop p _ _ hσ hτ
    rwa [show p.1 * (p.1⁻¹ * σ) = σ by group, show p.2 * (p.2⁻¹ * τ) = τ by group] at this
  rw [h1, h2]

/-- A locally constant function `Gal(Ω/K) × Gal(Ω/K) → Ωˣ` factors through
`Gal(L/K) × Gal(L/K)` and takes all its values in `L`, for one finite Galois subextension `L/K`.

The two conclusions come from different arguments —
`exists_intermediateField_eq_of_isLocallyConstant` for the first, and finiteness of the range of
a locally constant function on a compact space for the second — and are then combined by
replacing the two fields by their join, which is still finite and Galois over `K`: enlarging the
field shrinks its fixing subgroup, so the factorization survives. -/
theorem exists_finiteGaloisIntermediateField_of_isLocallyConstant
    (f : Gal(Ω/K) × Gal(Ω/K) → Ωˣ) (hf : IsLocallyConstant f) :
    ∃ L : FiniteGaloisIntermediateField K Ω,
      (∀ σ τ a b : Gal(Ω/K), a ∈ L.toIntermediateField.fixingSubgroup →
          b ∈ L.toIntermediateField.fixingSubgroup → f (σ * a, τ * b) = f (σ, τ)) ∧
        ∀ p : Gal(Ω/K) × Gal(Ω/K), ((f p : Ω) ∈ L.toIntermediateField) := by
  obtain ⟨E, hEfin, hEprop⟩ := exists_intermediateField_eq_of_isLocallyConstant f hf
  have := hEfin
  let L₁ : FiniteGaloisIntermediateField K Ω :=
    { normalClosure K E Ω with
      finiteDimensional := normalClosure.is_finiteDimensional K E Ω
      isGalois := IsGalois.normalClosure K E Ω }
  have : Finite (((fun u : Ωˣ => (u : Ω)) '' Set.range f) : Set Ω) :=
    (hf.range_finite.image _).to_subtype
  let L₂ : FiniteGaloisIntermediateField K Ω :=
    FiniteGaloisIntermediateField.adjoin K ((fun u : Ωˣ => (u : Ω)) '' Set.range f)
  refine ⟨L₁ ⊔ L₂, fun σ τ a b ha hb => ?_, fun p => ?_⟩
  · have hle : E ≤ (L₁ ⊔ L₂).toIntermediateField :=
      le_trans (IntermediateField.le_normalClosure E) (by exact le_sup_left)
    exact hEprop σ τ a b (IntermediateField.fixingSubgroup_antitone hle ha)
      (IntermediateField.fixingSubgroup_antitone hle hb)
  · have hmem : (f p : Ω) ∈ L₂.toIntermediateField :=
      FiniteGaloisIntermediateField.subset_adjoin K _ ⟨f p, Set.mem_range_self p, rfl⟩
    exact (show L₂ ≤ L₁ ⊔ L₂ from le_sup_right) hmem

omit [IsGalois K Ω] in
/-- The inflation of a `2`-cochain from a finite Galois subextension `L/K` to `Ω/K`: restrict
both arguments to `L` and push the value along `L → Ω`. -/
def inflation₂ (L : FiniteGaloisIntermediateField K Ω) (F : Gal(↥L/K) × Gal(↥L/K) → Lˣ) :
    Gal(Ω/K) × Gal(Ω/K) → Ωˣ := fun q =>
  Units.map (algebraMap ↥L Ω).toMonoidHom
    (F (AlgEquiv.restrictNormalHom ↥L q.1, AlgEquiv.restrictNormalHom ↥L q.2))

omit [IsGalois K Ω] in
/-- Inflation from a finite Galois subextension produces a locally constant function: the
restriction map `Gal(Ω/K) → Gal(L/K)` is continuous and `Gal(L/K)` is discrete. -/
theorem isLocallyConstant_inflation₂ (L : FiniteGaloisIntermediateField K Ω)
    (F : Gal(↥L/K) × Gal(↥L/K) → Lˣ) : IsLocallyConstant (inflation₂ L F) := by
  intro s
  exact (isOpen_discrete ((fun r : Gal(↥L/K) × Gal(↥L/K) =>
        Units.map (algebraMap ↥L Ω).toMonoidHom (F r)) ⁻¹' s)).preimage
    (((InfiniteGalois.restrictNormalHom_continuous
        L.toIntermediateField).comp continuous_fst).prodMk
      ((InfiniteGalois.restrictNormalHom_continuous
        L.toIntermediateField).comp continuous_snd))

/-- Pushing a unit of `L` along `L → Ω` is equivariant for the restriction `Gal(Ω/K) → Gal(L/K)`. -/
private theorem units_map_algebraMap_restrictNormalHom_smul {K Ω : Type*} [Field K] [Field Ω]
    [Algebra K Ω] (L : FiniteGaloisIntermediateField K Ω) (g : Gal(Ω/K)) (v : Lˣ) :
    Units.map (algebraMap ↥L Ω).toMonoidHom (AlgEquiv.restrictNormalHom ↥L g • v) =
      g • Units.map (algebraMap ↥L Ω).toMonoidHom v := by
  ext
  exact AlgEquiv.restrictNormal_commutes g ↥L (v : ↥L)

omit [IsGalois K Ω] in
/-- Inflation from a finite Galois subextension takes `2`-cocycles to `2`-cocycles. -/
theorem isMulCocycle₂_inflation₂ (L : FiniteGaloisIntermediateField K Ω)
    {F : Gal(↥L/K) × Gal(↥L/K) → Lˣ} (hF : IsMulCocycle₂ F) :
    IsMulCocycle₂ (inflation₂ L F) := by
  set ρ : Gal(Ω/K) →* Gal(↥L/K) := AlgEquiv.restrictNormalHom ↥L with hρ
  set ι : Lˣ →* Ωˣ := Units.map (algebraMap ↥L Ω).toMonoidHom with hι
  have hιsmul : ∀ (g : Gal(Ω/K)) (v : Lˣ), ι (ρ g • v) = g • ι v :=
    units_map_algebraMap_restrictNormalHom_smul L
  intro g h j
  simp only [inflation₂, ← hι, ← hρ, map_mul ρ, ← map_mul ι, hF (ρ g) (ρ h) (ρ j)]
  rw [map_mul ι, hιsmul]

/-- Every locally constant `2`-cocycle `Gal(Ω/K) × Gal(Ω/K) → Ωˣ` is inflated from a `2`-cocycle
on a finite Galois subextension `L/K` with values in `Lˣ`.

This is the degree-two analogue of the reduction to a finite level that proves Hilbert's theorem
90 for an infinite Galois extension, and it is the first step of the surjectivity argument of
[Stacks, Tag 03R7]. The field `L` is produced by
`exists_finiteGaloisIntermediateField_of_isLocallyConstant`; the cocycle `F` is then obtained by
descending `f` along the surjection `Gal(Ω/K) → Gal(L/K)`, whose kernel is `Gal(Ω/L)`, and its
cocycle identity is inherited from that of `f` because `L → Ω` is an injective
`Gal(Ω/K)`-equivariant map of unit groups. -/
theorem exists_isMulCocycle₂_inflation (f : Gal(Ω/K) × Gal(Ω/K) → Ωˣ)
    (hloc : IsLocallyConstant f) (hf : IsMulCocycle₂ f) :
    ∃ (L : FiniteGaloisIntermediateField K Ω) (F : Gal(↥L/K) × Gal(↥L/K) → Lˣ),
      IsMulCocycle₂ F ∧ inflation₂ L F = f := by
  obtain ⟨L, hfac, hval⟩ := exists_finiteGaloisIntermediateField_of_isLocallyConstant f hloc
  set ρ : Gal(Ω/K) →* Gal(↥L/K) := AlgEquiv.restrictNormalHom ↥L with hρ
  set ι : Lˣ →* Ωˣ := Units.map (algebraMap ↥L Ω).toMonoidHom with hι
  have hιsmul : ∀ (g : Gal(Ω/K)) (v : Lˣ), ι (ρ g • v) = g • ι v :=
    units_map_algebraMap_restrictNormalHom_smul L
  have hmem : ∀ p : Gal(Ω/K) × Gal(Ω/K), ∃ v : Lˣ, ι v = f p := by
    intro p
    have hne : (⟨(f p : Ω), hval p⟩ : ↥L.toIntermediateField) ≠ 0 := by
      simp only [ne_eq, ← ZeroMemClass.coe_eq_zero, Units.ne_zero, not_false_eq_true]
    exact ⟨Units.mk0 _ hne, Units.ext rfl⟩
  choose u hu using hmem
  have hker : ∀ g : Gal(Ω/K), ρ g = 1 → g ∈ L.toIntermediateField.fixingSubgroup := by
    intro g hg
    rw [← IntermediateField.restrictNormalHom_ker L.toIntermediateField]
    simpa [MonoidHom.mem_ker, ← hρ] using hg
  have hwd : ∀ g g' h h' : Gal(Ω/K), ρ g = ρ g' → ρ h = ρ h' → f (g, h) = f (g', h') := by
    intro g g' h h' hg hh
    have hg' : g⁻¹ * g' ∈ L.toIntermediateField.fixingSubgroup := by
      refine hker _ ?_
      simp [map_mul, map_inv, hg]
    have hh' : h⁻¹ * h' ∈ L.toIntermediateField.fixingSubgroup := by
      refine hker _ ?_
      simp [map_mul, map_inv, hh]
    rw [show g' = g * (g⁻¹ * g') by group, show h' = h * (h⁻¹ * h') by group]
    exact (hfac g h _ _ hg' hh').symm
  have hsurj : Function.Surjective ρ := AlgEquiv.restrictNormalHom_surjective Ω
  have hwd' : ∀ a b, f (Function.surjInv hsurj (ρ a), Function.surjInv hsurj (ρ b)) = f (a, b) :=
    fun a b => hwd _ _ _ _ (Function.surjInv_eq hsurj _) (Function.surjInv_eq hsurj _)
  refine ⟨L, fun q => u (Function.surjInv hsurj q.1, Function.surjInv hsurj q.2), ?_, ?_⟩
  · intro σ τ υ
    obtain ⟨g, rfl⟩ := hsurj σ
    obtain ⟨h, rfl⟩ := hsurj τ
    obtain ⟨k, rfl⟩ := hsurj υ
    refine Units.map_injective (algebraMap ↥L Ω).injective ?_
    rw [map_mul, map_mul, hιsmul, hu, hu, hu, hu]
    have e₁ : f (Function.surjInv hsurj (ρ g * ρ h), Function.surjInv hsurj (ρ k))
        = f (g * h, k) :=
      hwd _ _ _ _ (by rw [Function.surjInv_eq hsurj, map_mul])
        (Function.surjInv_eq hsurj (ρ k))
    have e₄ : f (Function.surjInv hsurj (ρ g), Function.surjInv hsurj (ρ h * ρ k))
        = f (g, h * k) :=
      hwd _ _ _ _ (Function.surjInv_eq hsurj (ρ g)) (by rw [Function.surjInv_eq hsurj, map_mul])
    rw [e₁, hwd' g h, hwd' h k, e₄]
    exact hf g h k
  · funext q
    simp only [inflation₂, ← hι, ← hρ, hu]
    exact hwd' q.1 q.2

/-- The finite-level data behind the coboundary reductions: if the cocycles at every finite Galois
level are coboundaries, a locally constant `2`-cocycle on `Gal(Ω/K)` is trivialised by the inflation
of a `1`-cochain `x` at a finite level `L`. -/
private theorem exists_inflation₁_trivialises
    (H : ∀ (L : FiniteGaloisIntermediateField K Ω) (F : Gal(↥L/K) × Gal(↥L/K) → Lˣ),
      IsMulCocycle₂ F → IsMulCoboundary₂ F)
    (f : Gal(Ω/K) × Gal(Ω/K) → Ωˣ) (hloc : IsLocallyConstant f) (hf : IsMulCocycle₂ f) :
    ∃ (L : FiniteGaloisIntermediateField K Ω) (x : Gal(↥L/K) → Lˣ), ∀ g h : Gal(Ω/K),
      g • Units.map (algebraMap ↥L Ω).toMonoidHom (x (AlgEquiv.restrictNormalHom ↥L h)) /
        Units.map (algebraMap ↥L Ω).toMonoidHom (x (AlgEquiv.restrictNormalHom ↥L (g * h))) *
        Units.map (algebraMap ↥L Ω).toMonoidHom (x (AlgEquiv.restrictNormalHom ↥L g)) =
        f (g, h) := by
  obtain ⟨L, F, hFcoc, hFeq⟩ := exists_isMulCocycle₂_inflation f hloc hf
  obtain ⟨x, hx⟩ := H L F hFcoc
  set ρ : Gal(Ω/K) →* Gal(↥L/K) := AlgEquiv.restrictNormalHom ↥L with hρ
  set ι : Lˣ →* Ωˣ := Units.map (algebraMap ↥L Ω).toMonoidHom with hι
  have hιsmul : ∀ (g : Gal(Ω/K)) (v : Lˣ), ι (ρ g • v) = g • ι v :=
    units_map_algebraMap_restrictNormalHom_smul L
  refine ⟨L, x, fun g h => ?_⟩
  have hFeq' : ι (F (ρ g, ρ h)) = f (g, h) := by
    simpa only [inflation₂, ← hι, ← hρ] using congrFun hFeq (g, h)
  change g • ι (x (ρ h)) / ι (x (ρ (g * h))) * ι (x (ρ g)) = f (g, h)
  rw [← hFeq', ← hx (ρ g) (ρ h)]
  simp only [map_mul, map_div, hιsmul]

/-- **Reduction of the degree-two vanishing to the finite levels.** If, for every finite Galois
subextension `L/K` of `Ω/K`, every `2`-cocycle `Gal(L/K) × Gal(L/K) → Lˣ` is a coboundary, then
every locally constant `2`-cocycle `Gal(Ω/K) × Gal(Ω/K) → Ωˣ` is a coboundary; that is,
`H²(Gal(Ω/K), Ωˣ) = 0` follows from `H²(Gal(L/K), Lˣ) = 0` for all finite Galois `L/K`.

The cocycle is inflated from a finite level by `exists_isMulCocycle₂_inflation`, the hypothesis
trivializes it there, and the inflation of the trivializing `1`-cochain trivializes it on
`Gal(Ω/K)`. -/
theorem isMulCoboundary₂_of_forall_finiteGalois
    (H : ∀ (L : FiniteGaloisIntermediateField K Ω) (F : Gal(↥L/K) × Gal(↥L/K) → Lˣ),
      IsMulCocycle₂ F → IsMulCoboundary₂ F)
    (f : Gal(Ω/K) × Gal(Ω/K) → Ωˣ) (hloc : IsLocallyConstant f) (hf : IsMulCocycle₂ f) :
    IsMulCoboundary₂ f := by
  obtain ⟨L, x, hx⟩ := exists_inflation₁_trivialises H f hloc hf
  exact ⟨fun g => Units.map (algebraMap ↥L Ω).toMonoidHom (x (AlgEquiv.restrictNormalHom ↥L g)),
    hx⟩

omit [IsGalois K Ω] in
/-- The inflation of a `1`-cochain from a finite Galois subextension `L/K` to `Ω/K`: restrict the
argument to `L` and push the value along `L → Ω`. It is locally constant, the restriction map
`Gal(Ω/K) → Gal(L/K)` being continuous and `Gal(L/K)` discrete — exactly as for
`Stacks.GaloisCohomology.isLocallyConstant_inflation₂`. -/
theorem isLocallyConstant_inflation₁ (L : FiniteGaloisIntermediateField K Ω)
    (x : Gal(↥L/K) → Lˣ) :
    IsLocallyConstant fun g : Gal(Ω/K) =>
      Units.map (algebraMap ↥L Ω).toMonoidHom (x (AlgEquiv.restrictNormalHom ↥L g)) := by
  intro s
  exact (isOpen_discrete ((fun r : Gal(↥L/K) =>
      Units.map (algebraMap ↥L Ω).toMonoidHom (x r)) ⁻¹' s)).preimage
    (InfiniteGalois.restrictNormalHom_continuous L.toIntermediateField)

/-- **Reduction of the degree-two vanishing to the finite levels, with a locally constant
trivialising cochain.** This is `Stacks.GaloisCohomology.isMulCoboundary₂_of_forall_finiteGalois`
with its witness's regularity recorded: the `1`-cochain that trivialises `f` is inflated from a
finite Galois subextension, hence locally constant.

Mathlib's `groupCohomology.IsMulCoboundary₂` asks for no regularity of the witness, and the
degree-two comparison between the cocycle and derived-functor descriptions of Galois cohomology
(`Stacks.GroupCohomology.isZero_continuousGroupCohomology_two_of_forall_isCoboundary`) needs it. So
the conclusion is spelled out rather than packaged as `IsMulCoboundary₂`. -/
theorem exists_isLocallyConstant_isMulCoboundary₂_of_forall_finiteGalois
    (H : ∀ (L : FiniteGaloisIntermediateField K Ω) (F : Gal(↥L/K) × Gal(↥L/K) → Lˣ),
      IsMulCocycle₂ F → IsMulCoboundary₂ F)
    (f : Gal(Ω/K) × Gal(Ω/K) → Ωˣ) (hloc : IsLocallyConstant f) (hf : IsMulCocycle₂ f) :
    ∃ x : Gal(Ω/K) → Ωˣ, IsLocallyConstant x ∧
      ∀ g h : Gal(Ω/K), g • x h / x (g * h) * x g = f (g, h) := by
  obtain ⟨L, x, hx⟩ := exists_inflation₁_trivialises H f hloc hf
  exact ⟨_, isLocallyConstant_inflation₁ L x, hx⟩

/-- **Reduction of the degree-two vanishing to the finite levels**, with the cochain condition
spelled as continuity rather than local constancy.

This is the same statement as `isMulCoboundary₂_of_forall_finiteGalois`: a Galois module carries
the discrete topology, and a map out of a topological space into a discrete space is continuous
exactly when it is locally constant. It is recorded separately so that the identification of the
cochains used here with the continuous ones is checked rather than asserted. -/
theorem isMulCoboundary₂_of_continuous_of_forall_finiteGalois [TopologicalSpace Ωˣ]
    [DiscreteTopology Ωˣ]
    (H : ∀ (L : FiniteGaloisIntermediateField K Ω) (F : Gal(↥L/K) × Gal(↥L/K) → Lˣ),
      IsMulCocycle₂ F → IsMulCoboundary₂ F)
    (f : Gal(Ω/K) × Gal(Ω/K) → Ωˣ) (hcont : Continuous f) (hf : IsMulCocycle₂ f) :
    IsMulCoboundary₂ f :=
  isMulCoboundary₂_of_forall_finiteGalois H f ((IsLocallyConstant.iff_continuous f).2 hcont) hf

set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000 in
-- `SeparableClosure K` unfolds to `separableClosure K (AlgebraicClosure K)`, and unfolding it is
-- needed to find the action of `Gal(L/K)` on `Lˣ` for `L` a subextension of it.
variable (K) in
/-- **Reduction of the degree-two vanishing to the finite levels, for the absolute Galois
group.** If `H²(Gal(L/K), Lˣ) = 0` for every finite Galois extension `L/K` inside `Kˢᵉᵖ`, then
every locally constant `2`-cocycle `Gal(Kˢᵉᵖ/K) × Gal(Kˢᵉᵖ/K) → (Kˢᵉᵖ)ˣ` is a coboundary, i.e.
`H²(Gal(Kˢᵉᵖ/K), (Kˢᵉᵖ)ˣ) = 0`.

This is the shape in which [Stacks, Tag 03R8] consumes degree `2`: its hypothesis is about the
Brauer groups of the finite extensions of `K`, and those are what compute the finite-level
groups `H²(Gal(L/K), Lˣ)` appearing here. Supplying that last identification is the content of
[Stacks, Tag 03R7] and is not proved in this file. -/
theorem isMulCoboundary₂_separableClosure_of_forall_finiteGalois
    (H : ∀ (L : FiniteGaloisIntermediateField K (SeparableClosure K))
        (F : Gal(↥L/K) × Gal(↥L/K) → Lˣ), IsMulCocycle₂ F → IsMulCoboundary₂ F)
    (f : Gal(SeparableClosure K/K) × Gal(SeparableClosure K/K) → (SeparableClosure K)ˣ)
    (hloc : IsLocallyConstant f) (hf : IsMulCocycle₂ f) : IsMulCoboundary₂ f :=
  isMulCoboundary₂_of_forall_finiteGalois H f hloc hf

end Stacks.GaloisCohomology
